-- Single-command layout: the root is both the program and its only
-- command, so two docstrings can describe it. Both must reach the help --
-- the module's says what the program is, the command's says what the one
-- thing it does does, and neither has anywhere else to appear.
--
-- The module epilogue also has to coexist with the command's own
-- positional and return blocks rather than replacing them.
--' A one-trick program
--' The trick is addition.
--' @epilogue
--' Examples:
--'   solo 1 2
module solo (add)

import root-py

--' Add two integers
add :: Int -> Int -> Int
add x y = x + y
